# .gitignore — br-ai-context-kit (skeleton)
#
# The entries below are the per-app / internal files removed from the skeleton. Onboarding regenerates
# them into this tree, so keep them ignored — nothing here should ever reach the public repo.

# --- internal planning (not part of the published kit) ---
/DEV_PLAN.md
.claude*

# --- LSP internal build artifacts (whole folder excluded) ---
/lsp/
/scratch/*

# --- per-app onboarding output: generated & confidential, never commit ---
/app/*
!/app/ONBOARDING.md
!/app/onboarding/
# only the kit's templates; STEP 1's config backups here are app-private.
# A new template needs its own line or it is silently ignored.
/app/onboarding/*
!/app/onboarding/context-kit-always-load.md
!/app/onboarding/copilot-instructions.md

# Already tracked null version - no need to keep updating it
/ERRORS.md/

# --- forward-looking hygiene for clones that onboard/compile a real app ---
# (not part of the diff; safe to trim. compiled BR objects + node deps)
*.br
*.brs
*.bro
*.wb
*.wbo
node_modules/

# --- BR ports of the Python generators: kit-testing instruments, never published ---
# The .brs ports themselves are covered by *.brs above. These are what a test RUN drops
# into the tree: a sandbox index (never the canonical brtree-index.json) and DIR scratch.

/dev/*
!/dev/*.md
!/dev/*.json
# --- the harness kit: the docs, the standard procedures and the driver ---
# /dev/* above ignores the whole FOLDER, so each of these needs its own
# line or it is silently left out of the published kit - which is what
# happened: nothing under dev/ai_access/ was tracked at all.
# BR itself is not here: it lives in dev/tools/ (see the dev/tools/ rules
# below and BR_launch.md, "The files the harness uses").
!/dev/ai_access/
/dev/ai_access/*
!/dev/ai_access/*.md
!/dev/ai_access/br_mcp_driver.exe
!/dev/ai_access/brls.exe
!/dev/ai_access/prc/
!/dev/ai_access/prc/*.prc
# allow access to the folder
!/dev/tools/
# but block unspecified content
/dev/tools/*
!/dev/tools/br*
/dev/tools/brconfig*
/dev/tools/*.go
!/dev/tools/*.gif
!/dev/tools/*.bmp
!/dev/tools/*.exe
!/dev/tools/*.dll
!/dev/tools/printer.sys
!/dev/tools/*.md
!/dev/tools/*.json
!/dev/tools/*.ps1

# --- brweb: files this app's repo keeps although the kit skeleton ignores them ---
# ScreenIO/FileIO reference sources the kit docs cite by line number (screenio-guide.md,
# APP-DEV-GUIDE.md §4), and the STEP 1 environment scripts.
!/dev/tools/screenio.br
!/dev/tools/screenio.brs
!/dev/tools/screenio-release-notes.txt
!/dev/tools/fileio.brs
!/dev/tools/fileio-release-notes.txt
!/app/env.cmd
!/app/onboarding/setx.cmd
# The harness MCP entry (../.mcp.json runs it) and the GUI ON config it starts BR with.
!/app/br_mcp.cmd
!/dev/tools/brconfig.ai_gui
